    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "c9b46828-a16a-5f9f-a53a-ab6535a44695",
      ":question/problem": "Find ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ for  $f(x)={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}-x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The function $f(x)$ is the sum of three power functions. So, we apply the sum rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}-x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{-2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =2{x}^{(2-1)}+(-2){x}^{(-2-1)}-1 \\\\  & =2{x}^{1}-2{x}^{-3}-1 \\\\  & =2{x}^{1}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
